These signaling pathways lead to the production of different sets of pro-inflammatory cytokines, respectively, via NF-κB transcription factor pathway activation, and via MAP kinases phosphorylation and subsequent activation of type I PI3-kinase/Akt and transcription factors AP-1 and CREB [24].

